  "geometry_source_note": "Front wishbone and steering coordinates extracted with the SolidWorks API from VD12-KIN-002-FVSA_FRONT.SLDPRT, user-selected 3D Hardpoints Autocross (Anti) sketch; contact patch uses the Wheel Front ground-level tire center. Sketch points transformed to part coordinates, converted from meters to inches, then model (X,Y,Z)=(part z,part x,-part y). Rocker and rod pickups remain from mk12 input coords - Sheet1.pdf with its assumed mapping (-sheet z,-sheet x,-sheet y); model-X rocker axis retained. Rear geometry, loads and sizing unchanged. Full native export and point mapping are stored in examples/sources/. Rear candidate: wishbones and toe link from VD12-KIN-002-FVSA_REAR.SLDPRT, 3D HARDPOINTS (ANTI + INBOARD BRAKES), selected provisionally to match the front anti layout. Model (X,Y,Z)=(part z-61,part x,-part y), inches. Existing 61-inch wheelbase retained. Rear contact patch from Wheel Front tire center; the construction-axis ground intercept is not the contact patch. Rear pushrod and rocker retain Mk11 coordinates because this part contains no replacements. Candidate is not active: rear_right case_4_brake_corner does not converge with this mixed geometry."
